---
// Moat.astro — the compounding memory (VISION §4.6). The same task, run twice:
//   COLD (first time): no memory → spec-first, write the decision, gate it.
//   WARM (later): the decision is recalled → one-shot.
// The differentiator is "compounds," not "magic" (§8) — honest framing, no overclaim.
//
// Two state cards with an animated → between them (CSS marquee on the arrow; the global
// reduced-motion off-switch freezes it to a static arrow). class="reveal".
//
// Color discipline: the WARM state is the "recalled" state — violet is allowed here (§5: violet =
// "warm/recalled" states), used on the warm card's accent + the badge. The arrow uses the brand
// gradient (amber→violet) to read as the journey from spark to network. No internal asset URLs.
---

<section class="moat section reveal" aria-labelledby="moat-title">
  <div class="container moat__inner">
    <header class="moat__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The moat</p>
      <h2 id="moat-title" class="moat__title">Memory compounds.</h2>
      <p class="moat__sub muted">
        Run the same task twice. The first time, Agentry has no prior decision, so it works
        spec-first — and writes down what it decided. The next time, that decision is recalled,
        and the same task routes one-shot. The system gets cheaper at the work it has already
        reasoned through.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="moat__flow">
      <article class="moat__state moat__state--cold">
        <p class="moat__when label">First run · cold</p>
        <p class="moat__task">
          <span class="moat__taskmark" aria-hidden="true">/agentry:go</span>
          "dedupe the import resolver"
        </p>
        <p class="moat__shape moat__shape--cold">spec-first</p>
        <p class="moat__detail muted">
          No prior decision. Shape the approach, gate it, build — then write the decision to memory
          with its provenance.
        </p>
      </article>

      <div class="moat__arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="moat__arrowline"></span>
        <span class="moat__arrowhead">→</span>
        <span class="moat__arrownote label">decision recalled</span>
      </div>

      <article class="moat__state moat__state--warm">
        <p class="moat__when label">Next run · warm</p>
        <p class="moat__task">
          <span class="moat__taskmark" aria-hidden="true">/agentry:go</span>
          "dedupe the import resolver"
        </p>
        <p class="moat__shape moat__shape--warm">one-shot</p>
        <p class="moat__detail muted">
          The recalled decision removes the unknown. The least process that wins is now a single
          bounded pass — no re-deriving what was already settled.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .moat__inner {
    max-width: 1080px;
  }

  .moat__head {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }

  .moat__head .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .moat__title {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .moat__sub {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* the two-state flow: cold → warm, with the arrow between */
  .moat__flow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .moat__state {
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 24px 26px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  /* warm = recalled: a violet wash + accent (§5 violet = warm/recalled state) */
  .moat__state--warm {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--violet) 38%, var(--line));
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--violet-dim), transparent 60%), var(--panel);
  }

  .moat__when {
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  .moat__task {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .moat__taskmark {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .moat__shape {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 26px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  /* cold shape: cyan = a "process" data tone (semantic, not decorative) */
  .moat__shape--cold {
    color: var(--cyan);
  }
  /* warm shape: violet = the recalled/action state */
  .moat__shape--warm {
    color: var(--violet-2);
  }

  .moat__detail {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* the arrow: brand-gradient head with a drifting shimmer line; reduced-motion freezes it */
  .moat__arrow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding-inline: 14px;
    min-width: 96px;
  }

  .moat__arrowline {
    width: 100%;
    height: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan), var(--violet));
    background-size: 200% 100%;
    animation: moat-flow 2.6s linear infinite;
  }

  @keyframes moat-flow {
    0% {
      background-position: 0% 0;
    }
    100% {
      background-position: -200% 0;
    }
  }

  .moat__arrowhead {
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 700;
    background: var(--brand);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    color: transparent;
    animation: moat-nudge 2.6s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes moat-nudge {
    0%,
    100% {
      transform: translateX(-2px);
    }
    50% {
      transform: translateX(4px);
    }
  }

  .moat__arrownote {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--faint);
    text-align: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* reduced-motion: a calm, static arrow (the global off-switch zeroes the animations; we also
     pin the gradient line to a stable frame so it doesn't read as a half-rendered streak) */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .moat__arrowline {
      animation: none !important;
      background-position: 0 0 !important;
    }
    .moat__arrowhead {
      animation: none !important;
      transform: none !important;
    }
  }

  /* responsive: stack into a vertical flow; the arrow rotates to point down */
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .moat__flow {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }
    .moat__arrow {
      flex-direction: row;
      gap: 12px;
      padding-block: 10px;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    .moat__arrowline {
      display: none;
    }
    .moat__arrowhead {
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .moat__arrowhead {
        animation: moat-nudge-v 2.6s ease-in-out infinite;
      }
    }
    @keyframes moat-nudge-v {
      0%,
      100% {
        transform: rotate(90deg) translateX(-2px);
      }
      50% {
        transform: rotate(90deg) translateX(4px);
      }
    }
  }
</style>
